00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.160
Balkan Insight reports that on the 30th of September,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.560
the court locked T-24's website

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.580
and its social accounts under Article 8 slash A,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.960
citing crime prevention and public order.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.920
The order named 108 AIN items

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.080
said to weaken the Turkish family structure

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.960
and to harm young people's development

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.320
on sexual orientation and gender identity.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:58.160
T-24, founded in 2009 and counted among the country's most red-quality outlets, said

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:03.540
it took all 118 pieces down inside a four-hour deadline. The whole site stayed blocked

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.820
anyway. Journalists and rights advocates call the wider sweep unprecedented, as blocks

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:14.820
that began with LGBTQ plus groups reach independent media and even posts on a stock market scandal.

