00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:53.040
The case on both sides is whether Google must open Android to rival AI services and

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.580
hand search data to competitors.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:59.900
Google has taken two digital markets act orders to the EU General Court in Luxembourg.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:05.760
Oliver Bethel, its senior director of competition, says people bring personal questions to Google

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.720
search and that the data order would force those queries out without enough anonymization.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.880
Google's strongest case is privacy and security.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:19.400
The orders it says would harm users because personal queries would not be anonymized enough.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:22.260
The commission says it will defend the orders in court.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:27.700
It says those orders already weigh the integrity and security of the features and protect end

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:28.840
users' personal data.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.620
Its reason is access.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:37.240
In July, it found outside AI services lacked Android tools that Gemini has, including a voice

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.780
key phrase that wakes an assistant.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:44.120
The specification order tells Google to open 11 specific features from the next Android

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.900
release in July 2027.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:51.300
A second order tells Google to share search data with other search providers and to include

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:55.760
AI chatbots that offer search, which the commission says were previously left out.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:00.580
The commission says that would make the sharing actually work and level the field with Google

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:06.760
search. DuckDuckGo says the EU anonymization framework is robust and that an appeal only

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.640
buys Google time. Both sides accept that the commission issued the two orders in July

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:16.640
and that Google is challenging them in the general court. Those orders tie the Android

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:23.280
changes to the platform release in July 2027. A sign of progress sits in Denmark's toy trade.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:30.060
EuroNews reports Lego's net profit was about 1.15 billion euros in the first half of this year.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:35.020
up 32% on the same month's last year as adults by toys for themselves.

